This statement is great for bouncing around a theory in a newsgroup but 
doesn't stand up as well to real world gaming. First, you'd have to find 
the daggers - wizards aren't generated with them. Granted, they are not 
too hard to find, but in the early game they are much more plentiful in 
the mines than in the main dungeon (varients of daggers like crude 
daggers and elven daggers appear, but I don't count those).

Second, you would want to determine the b/u/c status of the item in 
question; not hard so long as your pet hasn't perished (as mine did 
early in the game). If your pet has perished then you need an altar. 
Altars don't appear that often. Sometimes you get one before Sokoban but 
not always. I am rather adamant about discovering this for items.

Assuming I do Sokoban first and the mines second (which I find gives me 
better chances for survival) I will generally reach minetown around 
level 9. By then I have whacked enough beasties with a staff to get 
expert. I may have some daggers by then but have not had sufficient 
opportunity to id them to my level of satisfaction and use them enough 
to achieve a decent level of expertise. Also note that wizards start 
with some martial expertise with a staff (basic) but not with daggers 
(unskilled).

So until I get magicbane, I usually do not have sufficient impetus to 
fool with daggers and enhance my ability with them without severely 
limiting my combat chance. Again note that the idea of wizards casting 
spells all the time at everything doesn't work in actual games - but 
sounds good on r.g.r.n.

